gui.inventory.item.autoeat.name=automatic eating
gui.inventory.item.autoeat.tooltip=§eAutomatic eating§r\n§7Automatically find and eat food based on food threshold and keyword priority\n§7. \n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings§r
gui.inventory.other_feature.speed.tooltip=\n§7 Switch and configure the mobile acceleration function. \n§7 supports five modes: Ground, Air, Bhop, LowHop, and OnGround.
gui.inventory.item.auto_fishing.name=automatic fishing
gui.inventory.item.auto_fishing.tooltip=§eAutomatic fishing§r\n§7 automatically completes swinging the rod, waiting for the hook to bite, closing the rod and replenishing the rod. \n§7 supports settings such as retry when the float is missing, timeout rod replenishment, and durability protection. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings§r
gui.inventory.auto_fishing.on=§aAuto fishing: On
gui.inventory.item.fly.name=fly
gui.inventory.item.fly.tooltip=§b§lFlying§r\n§7 provides a variety of flight implementation methods, you can try them freely. \n§7 supports momentum flight, gliding flight, and pulse flight, \n§7 and can be configured with speed, automatic takeoff, no collision, anti-knockback and anti-stuck air kick. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings
gui.inventory.item.kill_aura.name=Killing Aura
gui.inventory.item.kill_aura.tooltip=§c§lKilling Aura§r\n§7Automatically locks on nearby targets and attacks. \n§7 Configurable whether to turn head, smooth steering, \n§7 attack range, target type and attack rhythm. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings
gui.inventory.kill_aura.on=§a Killing Aura: On
gui.inventory.fly.on=§aFlight: On
gui.inventory.item.mouse_detach.name=Mouse out of game
gui.inventory.item.mouse_detach.tooltip=§eThe mouse leaves the game§r\n§7Release/return the mouse. F3+P can disable pausing when losing focus\n§7 can be used in conjunction with "Monster Killing Data-Enable Free Adjustment". \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aSwitch escape/return
gui.inventory.item.autofollow.name=Automatically chase monsters
gui.inventory.item.autofollow.tooltip=§e automatically chases monsters §r\n§7 sets a patrol area. When the player \n exceeds the area, it will automatically return to the center point \n and start chasing monsters again. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings§r
gui.inventory.item.arena_config.name=arena setting
gui.inventory.item.arena_config.tooltip=§eArena settings§r\n§7New arena item handling system\n§7Supports multiple modes: black and white list, take-only mode\n§7Includes advanced functions such as anti-blocking and full backpack discarding
gui.inventory.item.conditional_execution.name=conditional execution
gui.inventory.item.conditional_execution.tooltip=§eConditional execution§r\n§7 sets an area. When the player enters the area, \n automatically starts executing the specified script sequence, and \n automatically stops when the player leaves. \n is usually used for automatic reentry copies. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings§r
gui.inventory.item.auto_escape.name=Automatic escape
gui.inventory.item.auto_escape.tooltip=§e automatically escapes §r\n§7 When detecting nearby entities of the specified type, \n§7 gives priority to terminating the currently executing sequence, and \n§7 executes the escape sequence immediately. \n§7 supports entity name black and white list, \n§7 and delayed follow-up sequence after escape is completed. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen settings§r
gui.inventory.item.keybind_manager.name=Shortcut key management
gui.inventory.item.keybind_manager.tooltip=§eShortcut key management§r\n§7 Set global shortcut keys for commonly used functions, \n§7 such as stop script, killing halo, automatic fishing, flying, etc.
gui.inventory.item.profile_manager.name=Configuration management
gui.inventory.item.profile_manager.tooltip=§eConfiguration Management§r\n§7Create, switch or delete different configuration schemes. \n§7Each configuration plan has an independent set of settings.
gui.inventory.item.chat_optimization.name=Chat box optimization
gui.inventory.item.chat_optimization.tooltip=§e Chat box optimization §r\n§7 opens the advanced chat settings interface, \n§7 includes smart copy, anti-swipe, \n§7 custom appearance and other super full functions.
gui.inventory.item.auto_pickup.name=Automatically pick up dropped objects
gui.inventory.item.auto_pickup.tooltip=§e Automatically pick up dropped objects §r\n§7 After entering the designated area, automatically find the path \n§7 and pick up all dropped objects. After completion, you can \n§7 selectively execute subsequent scripts. Mainly \n is mainly used for one-click group logging\n§bLeft click:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight click:§r §eOpen configuration§r
gui.inventory.item.auto_use_item.name=Use items silently
gui.inventory.item.auto_use_item.tooltip=§e Use items silently§r\n§7 Automatically find items from the shortcut bar according to rules and use them silently. \n§7 supports "contains/identical" matching and ignores name color codes. \n\n§bLeft button:§r §aMaster switch§r\n§bRight button:§r §eOpen configuration§r
gui.inventory.item.warehouse_manager.name=Intelligent warehouse management
gui.inventory.item.warehouse_manager.tooltip=§b§lSmart Warehouse Management§r\n§7Manage all warehouse areas, \n§7View the contents of scanned boxes, \n§7 and enable the one-click automatic deposit function.
gui.inventory.item.baritone_settings.name=Baritone settings
gui.inventory.item.baritone_settings.tooltip=§eBaritone settings§r\n§7Search and edit all Baritone parameters.\n§7Supports type filtering, modified-only view, reset, apply and save.
gui.inventory.item.baritone_command_table.name=Baritone command table
gui.inventory.item.baritone_command_table.tooltip=§eBaritone command table§r\n§7Search commands, usage and examples.\n§7Supports favorites, history refill and direct execution.
gui.inventory.item.baritone_parkour.name=Baritone parkour
gui.inventory.item.baritone_parkour.tooltip=§dBaritone Parkour§r\n§7 Independently manages settings related to Baritone parkour mode. \n§7 splits the parkour master switch and configuration from the normal Baritone setup. \n\n§bLeft click:§r §aSwitch parkour mode master switch§r\n§bRight click:§r §eOpen parkour configuration§r
gui.inventory.item.debug_settings.name=Debug settings
gui.inventory.item.debug_settings.tooltip=§eDebug settings§r\n§7 manages the debug log output switch of each module. \n facilitates locating problems.
gui.inventory.item.auto_evacuate.name=Automatic evacuation of the arena
gui.inventory.item.auto_evacuate.tooltip=§eSmart Evacuation§r\n§7 Automatically navigate to the evacuation point according to the on-screen prompts. \n\n§bLeft button: §r §7 Turn on/off §a automatic state machine §r. \n§b Right click: §r §7 Open the menu §c Manually select §r to evacuate the target.
gui.inventory.item.resolution_info.name=window resolution
gui.inventory.item.resolution_info.tooltip=§eWindow Resolution§r\n§7 displays the \n actual resolution and GUI scaling of the current Minecraft window.
gui.inventory.item.reload_paths.name=§e Refresh path configuration
gui.inventory.item.reload_paths.tooltip=§e Refresh path configuration §r\n§c§l [Developer feature] §r\n§7 Reloads all built-in and \n custom path JSON files from the hard drive without restarting the game.
gui.inventory.item.player_equipment.name=Get/View player equipment
gui.inventory.item.player_equipment.tooltip=§eGet/View player equipment§r\n§bLeft click:§r §7Copy the crosshair and point it at the player and open it for viewing. \n§b Right click: §r §7 Directly open the last copied equipment. \n
gui.inventory.item.packet_handler.name=Packet processing
gui.inventory.item.packet_handler.tooltip=§b§lPacket processing§r\n§7 opens the advanced packet tool, \n§7 is used to capture, analyze and simulate sending game packets.
gui.inventory.item.gui_inspector_manager.name=GUI recognition manager
gui.inventory.item.gui_inspector_manager.tooltip=§b§lGUI identification manager§r\n§7 captures the currently opened GUI snapshot in the background, \n§7 views buttons, slots, titles and element paths. \n§7 can directly copy the path required for container click/element positioning.
gui.inventory.item.performance_monitor.name=Performance monitoring
gui.inventory.item.performance_monitor.tooltip=§b§lPerformance monitoring§r\n§7 Check the execution time of each module, \n§7 and switch on and off performance-related functions individually.
gui.inventory.item.terrain_scanner.name=Terrain scan management
gui.inventory.item.terrain_scanner.tooltip=§eTerrain scan management§r\n§7 manages all saved terrain scan data. \n§7 can create new scans, view, rename or \n§7 delete scan files.
gui.inventory.item.memory_manager.name=memory manager
gui.inventory.item.memory_manager.tooltip=§b§lMemory Manager§r\n§7Opens the advanced memory analysis tool. \n§7 can create memory snapshots and compare the number of entities and block entities at different \n§7 time points. \n§7 is used to locate potential memory leaks.
gui.inventory.item.setloop.name=Number of cycles
gui.inventory.item.setloop.tooltip=§eNumber of loops§r\n§7Set the number of loop executions of the script. \n-1 indicates an infinite loop, 0 indicates no execution, and \n greater than 0 indicates a specified number of times.
gui.inventory.path_type.custom=custom path
gui.inventory.path_type.builtin=Built-in script
gui.inventory.path.tooltip=§e%s§r\n§8Type: %s\n§7Click to run this script sequence.
gui.inventory.loop.infinite=§e Unlimited
gui.inventory.loop.off=§cClose
gui.inventory.loop.count=§b%s times
gui.inventory.loop.progress=Number of cycles: %s/%s
gui.inventory.item.block_replacement.name=area block replacement
gui.inventory.item.block_replacement.tooltip=§eZone block replacement§r\n§7Manage replacement rules just like silent use item rules. \n§7 supports setting diagonal areas, visual selections, \n§7 scanning area block types, and replacing local display \n§7 with specified blocks without affecting the server. \n\n§bLeft click:§r §eOpen configuration\n§bRight click:§r §eOpen configuration
gui.inv_viewer.title=Item Editor (press F on hover to edit)
gui.inventory.item.baritone_flight_pathing.name=Flight pathing
gui.inventory.item.baritone_flight_pathing.tooltip=§b§lFlight pathing§r\n§7Uses only the player's existing flight capability and prefers direct routes.\n§7Obstacles are routed around and ground targets are approached safely.\n\n§bLeft click:§r §aToggle flight pathing§r\n§bRight click:§r §eOpen flight pathing settings§r
